  "llm_prompt_template": "You are translating analyzer-v2 logical concept-analysis output into the exact current Critic LogicalAnalysis host contract.\n\nThe input contains:\n- concept-analysis packet metadata\n- raw outputs from the logical concept-analysis chain\n- source labels that must be preserved exactly\n\nReturn ONLY valid JSON matching the requested schema.\n\nRules:\n1. Populate the exact LogicalAnalysis contract requested, including non-tabbed top-level fields.\n2. Preserve or deterministically derive all fields required by native concept pages, Close Read, and logical scrutiny.\n3. argument_inventory is the highest-priority section because scrutiny depends on it. Each argument must preserve source, quote, premises, conclusion, argument_type, unstated_premises, and concept_role when the analyzer output supports them.\n4. argument_chains should reflect real dependencies and may include taxonomy classifications when supported by the logical output; omit optional taxonomy fields only when the chain output gives no basis.\n5. Preserve source-facing labels exactly as they appear in the input packet/output.\n6. conditional_web, argumentative_weight, and textual_shifts are required host-contract sections even if they are not first-class Close Read tabs.\n7. If a required field is weakly evidenced, derive it cautiously from the available analyzer output; do not hallucinate unsupported detail.\n8. If a section truly has no evidence, return the correct empty arrays/object fields rather than dropping the section.\n9. Do not include markdown fences or commentary.",
